PREDICT3 -- #530 closing pass 5, Opus measuring seat (SECOND instance, finishing the walled seat's work).
Written BEFORE `noff' and `RWall' are built and BEFORE pitrows530c5.py has run on ANY binary.  This file's mtime is
the order proof.  Instrument: instrument2/pitrows530c5.py (150 rows, a PROTOTYPE session, NOT the shipped probe).
Clone /tmp/gxopus530c5 (verified cmp-clean on dev_lca.c, dev_pckbc.c AND dev_8253.c, no .MUTANT, binary -nt all three).

DERIVATION (dev_8253.c, read here, not taken from the brief):
  :143-147  ports 0x40/0x41/0x42 = relative_addr 0/1/2 = LANES 0/1/2 (0x40&3=0 ...).  0x43 = I8253_TIMER_MODE = LANE 3.
  :280-285  the flip-flop advance is INSIDE the counter case and fires on EVERY counter access, read and write, but
            ONLY while (mode_byte & 0x30) == I8253_TIMER_16BIT (0x30).  wr_msb toggles on writes, rd_msb on reads --
            SEPARATE per direction.
  :289-348  MODE (lane 3): a READ returns mode_byte with NO side effect and NO flip-flop advance; a repeated identical
            control-word WRITE is idempotent (mode_byte, counter_select, rd_msb=wr_msb=0).  => THE 8253 CANNOT CARRY
            LANE 3 IN EITHER DIRECTION.
  :320-321  a control word REWINDS that counter's two flip-flops -- which is what makes every phase self-starting.

PHASES (each ends with FLAT reads; only ONE access per phase goes through lca_isa, the SPARSE one):
  live  cw; flat ST 0x34; flat ST 0x12; flat RD r1; flat RD r2                 want r1=0x34 r2=0x12
  PS X  cw; lca ST X (width w); flat ST 0x12; flat RD r1; flat RD r2           want r1=X    r2=0x12
  PL L  cw; flat ST L; flat ST 0x12; lca LD (width w); flat RD r1              want dlv=L   r1=0x12
  PW    cw; flat ST 0x5a; flat ST 0x12; lca LD (LDQ); flat ST 0x77; RD r1; r2  want r1=0x12 r2=0x77
  X and L each run at 0x00 and 0x5a (the zero/nonzero DATA partition, per cell, not as a marginal).
  Counters 0/1/2 at widths 1/2/4/8; tails 7/6/5/3 at port 0x40 via SP(0x3f)+0x1f/0x1e/0x1d/0x1b.

LEG      EDIT                                                        PREDICTED  RED ROWS (exact families)
