RWall    NEW: read arm + an unconditioned added MEM_WRITE of the      140/150   pw x10 ONLY.  PL is BLIND to an added
         fetched byte (the 4th cell of the class's 2x2, ungated)                 WRITE: rd_msb and wr_msb are separate
                                                                                 and the write-back rewrites the same
                                                                                 half with the same value
RWtail   the same gated to len 3/5/6/7 (BUILT)                        146/150   pw at the two TAIL cells only = 4

WHAT THE PREDICTIONS ASSERT, so a miss is informative:
 1. The store-side row (PS) detects ONE EXTRA ACCESS OF EITHER DIRECTION and cannot tell a doubled store from a
    phantom read -- WWall and Wpure must score IDENTICALLY, row for row.
 2. The read-side row (PL) detects an extra READ and is BLIND to an added WRITE -- RWall must leave every PL row green.
 3. Only PW sees the added write, and it sees it because it forces a LATER STORE whose half the write-back moved.
 4. Lane 3 is unreachable on this channel in BOTH directions -- cdxZL3 and W23 must be 150/150.
 5. The data partition is rowed PER CELL: dNZtail must red at X=0x5a and stay green at X=0x00 in the SAME tail cell.
